V: Kenyan Primary School Management System (SaaS Architecture Blueprint)
Production-Grade Event-Driven Architecture Document for Competency-Based Curriculum (CBC) & Local Financial Integrations

1. Executive System Overview & Architectural Strategy
----------------------------------------------------

This document outlines the system architecture for V, an enterprise-grade,
high-volume Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) School Management System engineered
specifically for the Kenyan primary education framework.

Traditional architectures fail in the Kenyan primary school tech market due to
two highly volatile operational realities:
1. The M-Pesa Concurrency Problem: Sudden, high-volume transactional spikes
   hitting payment collection webhooks simultaneously during school reopening weeks.
2. The End-of-Term Grading Rush: Severe, concurrent write-heavy performance hits
   on the server infrastructure when thousands of teachers upload continuous
   assessment rubrics at the same time.

To solve these constraints without driving cloud resource bills past subscription
profitability metrics, V abandons monolithic synchronous APIs. Instead, it
utilizes an asynchronous Event-Driven Architecture (EDA) built around a
microservices pattern, clean data ingestion pipelines, and strict multi-tenant
row-level data security frameworks.

2. Comprehensive System Architecture Blueprint
----------------------------------------------

                      +---------------------------------------+
                      |         Cloud Ingestion Layer         |
                      |   Go / Gin-Engine Gateway (Lean API)  |
                      +-------------------+-------------------+
                                          |
                        Publish Event     v     Asynchronous Pipe
                      +---------------------------------------+
                      |          Apache Kafka Broker          |
                      |  Topics: mpesa.payments | cbc.grading |
